WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
Dr. Dolittle and Polynesia arrived on the beach.

2
00:00:04.181 --> 00:00:08.657
Tommy was so happy to see the doctor that he began to cry.

3
00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:11.937
"Hush, now," the doctor said, comforting him.

4
00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:14.539
"It’s good to have you back, Dr. Dolittle,"

5
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.404
Charles said as he brushed away a tear.

6
00:00:18.405 --> 00:00:23.382
"We must get going before the natives find you are missing," said Polynesia.

7
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:25.298
"Will the people be all right?"

8
00:00:25.299 --> 00:00:28.539
the doctor asked, looking back toward the huts.

9
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.258
"Of course," answered Long Arrow.

10
00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:33.222
"They already have a chief.

11
00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:36.508
Do not worry, I will explain to them."

12
00:00:36.509 --> 00:00:40.679
"You’re not coming with us?" the doctor said in surprise.

13
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.548
"I’m afraid not, my friend," the Indian said sadly.

14
00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:46.786
"My journey is different from yours.

15
00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:50.035
You must go your way, and I must go mine."

16
00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:52.902
The two men did not speak for a minute.

17
00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:56.809
"Will we ever meet again?" asked Dr. Dolittle.

18
00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:02.639
"As long as the eagles soar, our paths shall cross," replied Long Arrow.

19
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.459
A loud splash came from the waters.

20
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.150
"He is here," Polynesia said.

21
00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.290
"Who is?" asked the doctor.

22
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:12.520
"Remember what the fidgit said?"

23
00:01:12.521 --> 00:01:15.378
Tommy grabbed the doctor’s hand excitedly.

24
00:01:15.379 --> 00:01:19.447
"He spoke about the great glass sea snail?"

25
00:01:19.448 --> 00:01:22.577
Tommy led the doctor toward the edge of the water.

26
00:01:22.578 --> 00:01:27.695
Dr. Dolittle stopped in his tracks and gasped at the creature before him.

27
00:01:27.696 --> 00:01:32.156
It was an enormous snail, the size of two large houses.

28
00:01:32.157 --> 00:01:36.722
Its shell was transparent and shone like a million diamonds.

29
00:01:36.723 --> 00:01:40.408
"It’s beautiful!" sighed the doctor.

30
00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:42.980
"How did you find it?"

31
00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:50.841
"When we told Long Arrow you wanted to learn shellfish language," explained Tommy, "Long Arrow went in search of the snail."

32
00:01:50.842 --> 00:01:53.717
Dr. Dolittle smiled at Long Arrow.

33
00:01:53.718 --> 00:01:58.982
"Now you can learn the language on your way back home," said Tommy.

34
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:04.103
"What? Will the snail come with us?" the doctor said, confused.

35
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:08.145
The snail let out a loud groan and shook its huge body.

36
00:02:08.146 --> 00:02:11.554
The bottom of its shell came away from its body.

37
00:02:11.555 --> 00:02:15.464
Dr. Dolittle’s eyes grew big with excitement.

38
00:02:15.465 --> 00:02:20.225
"You and your friends can ride inside the shell," Long Arrow explained.

39
00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:24.211
"The snail will take you on an underwater journey."

40
00:02:24.212 --> 00:02:27.424
Dr. Dolittle wiped a tear from his eye.

41
00:02:27.425 --> 00:02:31.253
"How can I ever thank you?" he said with emotion.

42
00:02:31.254 --> 00:02:33.814
"You are my dearest friend."

43
00:02:33.815 --> 00:02:37.085
Dr. Dolittle blew his nose.

44
00:02:37.086 --> 00:02:41.949
"You have made all my dreams come true."

45
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.178
Tommy felt a lump in his throat.

46
00:02:44.179 --> 00:02:46.008
He looked around the island.

47
00:02:46.009 --> 00:02:48.234
The sun was starting to come up.

48
00:02:48.235 --> 00:02:53.541
He realized that he had learned much more on this voyage than he had ever

49
00:02:53.542 --> 00:02:58.179
expected. But he also realized how much he missed his parents and

50
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.954
Puddleby. He was ready to go

51
00:03:01.955 --> 00:03:05.420
home. It was very sad to say good-bye to Long

52
00:03:05.421 --> 00:03:08.409
Arrow. He had a gift for each of his new

53
00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.089
friends. To Charles he gave a beautiful stone with a red dot in the

54
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.286
middle. To Tommy he gave a large eagle’s

55
00:03:16.287 --> 00:03:20.180
feather. Tommy wore it in his hair, just like Long

56
00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:24.715
Arrow. For Polynesia, Long Arrow had a tiny necklace made of

57
00:03:24.716 --> 00:03:27.689
flowers. She wore it proudly around her

58
00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.361
neck. And finally, to Dr. Dolittle Long Arrow gave his

59
00:03:32.362 --> 00:03:37.203
pouch. "I can’t accept this," the doctor said, his voice

60
00:03:37.204 --> 00:03:40.997
choking. "It is my most treasured item," said the

61
00:03:40.998 --> 00:03:44.253
Indian, "and I want my most treasured friend to have

62
00:03:44.254 --> 00:03:49.405
it." The two friends cried as they finally said

63
00:03:49.406 --> 00:03:53.699
good-bye. Dr. Dolittle and his friends climbed into the sea snail’s

64
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.961
shell. Inside the shell, it was comfortably

65
00:03:56.962 --> 00:04:02.314
warm. There were no chairs, but Tommy found that the snail’s back was soft to sit

66
00:04:02.315 --> 00:04:04.186
on. He looked

67
00:04:04.187 --> 00:04:09.476
outside. It felt strange to view the world from inside a

68
00:04:09.477 --> 00:04:13.885
shell. After everyone was settled in, the snail groaned once

69
00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:18.629
again. Its shell locked in place and slowly it moved into the

70
00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:24.773
water. Dr. Dolittle and his friends waved to Long Arrow as they disappeared below the

71
00:04:24.774 --> 00:04:29.142
waves. "Now the real voyage begins!" Charles shouted

72
00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:35.168
joyfully. Yes, returning home was yet another

73
00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:39.641
adventure. After returning to Puddleby, Tommy’s life changed quite a

74
00:04:39.642 --> 00:04:42.737
bit. He could now speak more animal

75
00:04:42.738 --> 00:04:46.348
languages. He was no longer afraid of any kind of

76
00:04:46.349 --> 00:04:50.959
animal. And he was certain that he wanted to be an animal doctor when he grew

77
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.595
up. But some things would never

78
00:04:54.596 --> 00:04:57.133
change. "Tommy! Come listen to

79
00:04:57.134 --> 00:05:02.765
this!" the doctor would shout excitedly, pulling his head out of the shellfish

80
00:05:02.766 --> 00:05:04.757
tank. "I think I’ve got

81
00:05:04.758 --> 00:05:10.046
it!" Whenever Charles came to visit, Dr. Dolittle and his friends would talk about their

82
00:05:10.047 --> 00:05:14.327
trip. The other pets never got tired of hearing all the exciting

83
00:05:14.328 --> 00:05:18.174
stories. But Tommy was ready for a new

84
00:05:18.175 --> 00:05:23.184
voyage. During one of Charles’ visits, Dr. Dolittle looked at Tommy and

85
00:05:23.185 --> 00:05:27.694
winked. It seemed as if Dr. Dolittle were ready

86
00:05:27.695 --> 00:05:30.551
too. Tommy thought of places they could

87
00:05:30.552 --> 00:05:32.978
travel. It didn’t matter where they

88
00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:42.390
